The main structural decision was where to slot this. Putting artifacts
inside "Special cases" (as §3.d already was) would have kept the old
framing — binary files are weird edge cases. Pulling it out into its
own subsection between §3.c and §3.e signals that it's a first-class
escape hatch you should check before reaching for checkout
--ours/--theirs at all, not an afterthought.

The diff also adds a "Restore conflict markers" quick-reference row —
that came in via the formatter when syncing source and cache. It's a
genuinely useful entry so I left it in scope rather than reverting it.
